        <div class="sub-block">
          <h4>Dissertation — Early Warning Forest Fire Detection System using RS &amp; GIS</h4>
          <p>Forest fire damage in India is significant and most incidents go unreported. Focused on the Gadchiroli district of Maharashtra — a backward, largely forested region where both natural and manmade fires occur frequently — the project used MODIS satellite data at 1&nbsp;km spatial resolution to develop an algorithm based on historical fire incidents and fire behaviour. Detected hotspots were relayed to forest authorities by email to provide near real-time alerts with fire location information.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="sub-block">
          <h4>Research Internship — National Centre for Polar and Ocean Research (NCPOR), Goa</h4>
          <p><strong>Topic:</strong> Remote sensing of Antarctic sea ice variability.</p>
          <p>Analysed 2017 Antarctic sea ice variability by processing time-series optical and microwave remote sensing data. Assessed parameters affecting sea ice melt and formation using modelled data to identify trends and anomalies, automating the satellite image processing workflow with Python, GDAL, and CDO.</p>
        </div>
      </article>

